{
  "repository": "sv5byp/FTFlow",
  "tag": "r182",
  "title": "FTflow r182 - Persistent CQ/Call selection and CW improvements",
  "body": "FTflow r182 continues the complete FTFlow line, including the existing weak-signal modes, RTTY Bot and CW Bot.\n\nChanges since the public r172\n- CQ<->Call is a persistent checkbox. Auto CQ, Auto Call, Normal, temporary pauses and restart keep the operator's choice. Only explicitly ticking/unticking changes it; default ON for a missing preference, saved OFF respected. Normal pauses alternation without clearing the selection. Restoring a selection does not start PTT.\n- DF tolerance changes require the operator's explicit Apply. Pending edits are separate; waterfall actions cannot change active or pending DF. Each mode remembers its last applied value. The animated green RX progress line was removed; red TX progress remains.\n- CW selected RX AFC can search within +/-200Hz of the chosen RX with TX fixed, retaining competing-signal/noise/hold guards. Optional word spacing handles additional unambiguous CQ/DE/callsign and 73 combinations by inserting spaces only. It does not correct wrong decoded characters or guarantee CW Skimmer accuracy.\n- Up to eight simultaneous CW receivers, more stable rows for small frequency drift, and row cleanup after60seconds without a nearby carrier. Double-clicking a decoded row/station moves RX and TX together without transmitting; the active automatic-QSO partner remains protected.\n- CW waterfall Time span0.50-3.00seconds in finer steps; adjustable waterfall height in both Bots. RTTY AFC speed is adjustable. Received-text selection remains usable while new text arrives; Callsign/RST/QTH/Name/Locator assignment menus, Copy/Clear, decoded-station history clearing and slashed zero improve operation. Manual CW/RTTY remain public; code-granted automation/slot rights retain their expiry behavior.\n- Clock synchronization defaults OFF for new profiles and saves the user's choice. When enabled, the interval is30minutes. The updated helper recognizes fresh completed Windows tasks and retains after-synchronization verification; errors are not hidden. The menu shows measured milliseconds and time since the last verified synchronization.\n\nUpdate existing FTFlow\nUse Help > Check for updates in versions that support signed automatic updates. Accept and allow restart after transmission/automatic QSO has stopped. The signed update and embedded verified companions deliver the clock helper, CW model and automation runtime. Settings, activation records, contacts and logs are retained. Existing startup-check preferences remain respected. r171 and other builds without an updater menu require the full portable download once.\n\nNew installation\nExtract the ENTIRE FTflow-SV5BYP-r182-Windows-x64-portable.zip into a new folder and run FTFlow.exe. Keep every included file/subfolder together. Configure your own callsign, audio devices and radio/PTT connection. No separate installer is required. For manual installation, do not copy only an EXE.\n\nOptional clock synchronization requires Windows10/11 and Windows PowerShell5.1; first explicit activation may request Windows permission. No task is installed/run merely by extracting the package with synchronization OFF. Program and companion updates are separate recoverable transactions; backups are retained under update-backups. If companion deployment is blocked by locked files or folder permissions, close interfering tools and restart to retry.\n\nValidation\nThe r182 application passed344 fresh software checks, including persistent ON/OFF choice, quick buttons, restart without PTT, inherited DF and CW checks. Prior r181 also passed2980 checks for CW spacing/capture and regressions. Generated signals and existing recordings do not establish universal on-air accuracy. No physical radio/audio/CAT/PTT operation or privileged clock correction/task installation was performed during development. Corresponding source accompanies this release.\n\nCredits\nBased on MSHV by Hrisimir Hristov, LZ2HV (GNU GPL). DeepCW model by VE3NEA (MIT). Original licenses, credits and map attribution are retained. No proprietary CW Skimmer code is included. SHA256SUMS.txt lists release asset checksums.\n",
